<id/01/0182/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mahogany - Furniture, Hardwoods or Veneers"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <customs-1866/timber/#concept> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_sawn_lumber/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a well-known valuable furniture wood, chiefly imported from Honduras, where it is obtained from a large forest tree, the *Swietenia Mahagoni*. African mahogany is the wood of *Khaya senegalensis*. The wood of the Toon-tree (*Cedrela Toona*) is sometimes called Indian mahogany. Our imports of mahogany average about 33,000 tons per annum. The stringent bark is used in the West Indies as a substitute for cinchona, but contains no alkaline principle. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 249]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "0182" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mahogany - Furniture, Hardwoods or Veneers"@en ;
